Primary fraud controls:
- Automated and real-time fraud monitoring and detection systems with transaction velocity checks or thresholds, monitoring of mobile device and account information changes, geolocation and behavioral anomalies, and blacklist screening;
- Customer authentication controls;
- 24-hour Transaction Pause Period after applying key account changes

Customer/user protection:
- Temporary holding of funds subject of a disputed transaction; 
- Real-time customer notification through secure channels;
- Mechanisms to enable account holders to verify the identity of recipients of fund transfers; 
- Self-service facility that enables account holders to suspend their account, block outgoing financial transactions and prevent unauthorized changes to account information
- Money lock feature
- Customizable transaction limits
- Consumer awareness program
